docs/modules/ROOT/pages/upgrade.adoc:50:SDK 0.10.5 deprecated the `reentrant` entrypoint guard because high-level calls now flush storage before transferring control. In SDK 0.10.10, the guard is still enabled by default. Enable the library's `reentrant` feature for contracts whose external callback must call back into the same contract; this forwards the SDK feature and disables the guard. The flash-mint example enables it by default because borrower callbacks commonly read or call the lender token during the loan. Consumers should enable it only when their contract needs reentrant calls and should still follow checks-effects-interactions.
